WEBVTT

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:08.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday the eighth of July. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:09.199 --> 00:00:14.800
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, got you. Only just made it in, mind. Traffic on the ring road was dreadful.</v>

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:22.769
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same. Traffic on the ring road, then somebody trying to squeeze across three lanes. Lovely start.</v>

00:00:23.899 --> 00:00:26.699
<v Jamie Brennan>Probably saved themselves about four seconds as well.</v>

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.340
<v Hannah Price>Still less frustrating than the football last night. Sat through all that for nothing.</v>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.880
<v David Whitfield>That's why I only watch the highlights. Disappointment, but quicker.</v>

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:45.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes breakfast radio. Finished work first, then what we actually need to agree.</v>

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:52.619
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, so I signed off the inspection on the turbine one compressor on Tuesday. That's closed.</v>

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that's yesterday's sign-off, not something going round again.</v>

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:02.119
<v David Whitfield>And I finished the repair on the number two bearing last night. All done.</v>

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:08.209
<v Marcus Hale>Ah, right. I wasn't sure whether that was still hanging over from nights.</v>

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.170
<v Priya Raman>I finished the repair on the HV board last night as well. That one's complete.</v>

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.359
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Anything from nights that's just for awareness?</v>

00:01:21.709 --> 00:01:29.409
<v Priya Raman>Um, noticed the CT1 was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation, nothing outstanding from that.</v>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.530
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, those little blips make the handover sound worse than it is sometimes.</v>

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:37.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, keeping that as an observation.</v>

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.680
<v Marcus Hale>Also saw the pressure on the fire alarm panel dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.250
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, you said it came back without anyone doing anything?</v>

00:01:51.959 --> 00:01:56.859
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, on its own. Just saying what I saw, not asking for another job.</v>

00:01:58.769 --> 00:02:02.969
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's an observation, not a new action out of this meeting.</v>

00:02:03.379 --> 00:02:11.080
<v Marcus Hale>And we're still waiting on parts for the AC1, nothing we can do until they arrive. Same blocker, no progress to report.</v>

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.659
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, that's the existing parts hold. Nothing new to add from stores.</v>

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, still blocked then.</v>

00:02:20.629 --> 00:02:30.080
<v Tomasz Nowak>One other thing: we were going to replace the belt on the pick and place on two but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:35.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, that's off this round. Not counting it as work for today.</v>

00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:40.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you check the guarding on the palletizer today at 2pm? It's urgent.</v>

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>At two, yeah? Not just sometime before the end of the shift?</v>

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:53.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Today at 2pm, yes. It's urgent, so that's the one I need kept firm.</v>

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:58.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. I'll check the guarding on the palletizer today at 2pm.</v>

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:07.810
<v Sarah Okafor>And Tomasz, can you recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve by tomorrow morning? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:03:08.699 --> 00:03:17.449
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, sorry, I can't take that as well. With the guarding and the time I've got available, I'd be promising something I can't fit in.</v>

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:26.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Dave, can you take that instead—recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve by tomorrow morning? Still fairly important.</v>

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:34.310
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll take it from Tomasz. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve by tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:36.419 --> 00:03:41.319
<v Priya Raman>Just the sensor calibration we're talking about, rather than work on the valve itself?</v>

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.139
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, just recalibrating the sensors. That's what I'm accepting.</v>

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Dave owns that one now, not Tomasz.</v>

00:03:51.219 --> 00:04:00.669
<v Tomasz Nowak>While we're on tomorrow, I'll do a site visit at Northfield with the contractor tomorrow. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:04:02.919 --> 00:04:08.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz. Northfield with the contractor tomorrow, agreed. Separate from the calibration you've handed over.</v>

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:14.280
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. I can commit to the visit, just couldn't squeeze that calibration in as well.</v>

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.689
<v Jamie Brennan>A diary with actual limits. Radical stuff.</v>

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.269
<v Tomasz Nowak>Someone ought to tell Teams. It thinks every white square is an invitation.</v>

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.300
<v Hannah Price>Um, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test on Friday. Fairly important, so I'm keeping that one definite.</v>

00:04:32.009 --> 00:04:39.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah Price. Monthly fire alarm test on Friday is yours. That's the routine test, separate from the panel observation earlier.</v>

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:47.920
<v Hannah Price>Yes, exactly. I'll do the monthly test on Friday, not taking on a separate investigation from that comment.</v>

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.769
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, understood. Didn't mean to muddy the two together.</v>

00:04:53.439 --> 00:04:58.339
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you replace the seals on the boiler feed pump tomorrow? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:09.589
<v Priya Raman>I can own it, but—sorry, just to get this in—we're still waiting on parts for the boiler feed pump, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:22.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, understood. The seal replacement is still due tomorrow, normal priority. I'm not saying the parts are here; the physical work is blocked until they arrive. Are you happy to take ownership on that basis?</v>

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:33.670
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, accepted. I'll replace the seals on the boiler feed pump, due tomorrow, normal priority. But I can't start the replacement until those parts arrive.</v>

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:41.779
<v Jamie Brennan>And we've not got anything in this conversation that clears that parts hold. Just so it doesn't sound like we have.</v>

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:48.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. PR owns the replacement; the parts blocker remains. No separate new job off the blocker.</v>

00:05:51.019 --> 00:06:01.519
<v Marcus Hale>There's still a need to take vibration readings on the Gas Turbine 2 by the end of the week. Low priority. I'm raising it, but I can't take it myself.</v>

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:09.879
<v David Whitfield>I can't commit to that one either. Don't put my name against it just because I've got the calibration.</v>

00:06:11.709 --> 00:06:14.509
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nor mine, sorry. No room to promise that.</v>

00:06:15.879 --> 00:06:18.680
<v Priya Raman>Same here. I'm not volunteering for the readings.</v>

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:27.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, vibration readings on the Gas Turbine 2, by the end of the week, low priority. Needed, but nobody's taken them.</v>

00:06:28.939 --> 00:06:34.540
<v Hannah Price>Not one I can pick up either. Sorry, I was nodding at the deadline, not offering.</v>

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:42.050
<v Sarah Okafor>That's fine. It stays unassigned. A nod on a tiny Teams tile isn't an acceptance.</v>

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:49.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Good rule. Half the time I'm just trying to get my chair to stop sinking.</v>

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:58.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we've got the agreed work, the parts holds are still holds, and the cancelled belt job stays out. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:07:00.189 --> 00:07:01.389
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>
